WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.270
Before an aircraft is refuelled,

2
00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:06.250
a crew member clips a metal wire
from the plane to the ground.

3
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:09.650
Only then does the fuel start
to flow along the hose into the

4
00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:10.930
wing tanks.

5
00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:14.450
Nothing is plugged in, and
nothing is switched on.

6
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:18.710
So why would fuel simply flowing
through a pipe be dangerous?

7
00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:22.370
In this mission, you'll find
out when static charge becomes a

8
00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:25.410
danger, how earthing
keeps people safe,

9
00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:30.150
and how static is put to good
use, for example in printers.

10
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:34.490
Your mission: find out why
flowing fuel can be dangerous.
